WEBVTT

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.620
The concert that was supposed 
to happen on the Zwei Islands

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.320
has been officially moved to next month.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.630
As such, we'd like to ask <i>Little Garden</i>,
who will handle security for the event,

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.130
for a little favor of sorts.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.050
There's someone Sakura 
would like as her bodyguard.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.890
<b>Bodyguard</b>

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.330
Hayato!

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.680
Now, Hayato!

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.080
Right!

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:29.380
Wait!

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:33.290
Damn it. I'm out of energy...

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:35.630
Just kidding.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.220
<i>He's got a muzzle there?!</i>

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.680
<i>Focus...</i>

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.710
<i>Don't let it take over.</i>

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:48.520
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.330
Fritz!

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.010
You've got me.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.150
I surrender.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.540
That was amazing! They're all too good!

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:11.330
Kisaragi-kun in particular was so fast at the end,
 I couldn't even see him!

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.240
Yeah!

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.930
People in Selections are 
really on a different level.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:16.670
Yeah!

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.300
Good work, Hayato.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:22.480
You're able to control
your Variant pretty well now.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.180
Yeah, I hope so.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:28.480
I didn't think you'd cut through my attack.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:34.580
I thought we'd gotten stronger
in the month since we came to this school,

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.820
but I guess getting into Selections 
is still a pipe dream.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.060
That's not true.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:45.570
Not many people could force Hayato
into his full-body armament.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.940
Yeah, I guess!

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.390
Just goes to show that 
we're getting stronger too.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:53.460
Yeah!

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.250
Wait! Stop patting me on the head.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.040
<i>Kisaragi Hayato,</i>

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.720
<i>Claire-sama calls for you.</i>

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.550
<i>You have a Selections mission.</i>

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.720
A bodyguard for Kirishima Sakura?

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.490
She supposedly requested you herself.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:15.020
She'd like you to be there for the concert 
on the Zwei Islands next weekend.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.440
Why me?

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.730
I didn't get an exact answer for that.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:26.660
But so long as the Savage may still be
lurking on the Zwei Island chain,

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.030
all the VIPs there need protection.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:34.860
And in fact, we detected seven Savages
during our action last month.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.540
But we only fought three of them.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:39.740
That's correct.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.770
The other four were said to have been
shot down before they made landfall.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.180
However, we found the remains 
of only one of them.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.720
So they might be up and about somewhere?

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.520
Another three of those monsters?

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.040
It could be a dangerous mission.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.870
Kisaragi Hayato, what do you intend to do?

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:08.410
I accept.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:10.910
Please let me do this.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.870
Good answer.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:16.530
You'll be giving up your weekend,

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.500
so you should receive some moderate pay.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.210
Is there anything else 
you'd like to ask for?

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.920
Oh, in that case,

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.760
there is one thing...

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.100
Oh, Nii-san!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.310
What?!

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.810
You're going to be Sakura-san's bodyguard?!

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.270
K-Karen, you're being too loud.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:44.750
I... I'm sorry.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.860
Hold on a second. 
I need to take a deep breath.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.130
This all seems like a dream.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.930
You get to see Sakura-san...

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:59.410
I'd love to see her too, just once.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:00.450
You'll get your wish.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:00.960
Huh?

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:05.170
I had them get you a ticket for the concert.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.290
What? Really?!

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:07.970
Yeah.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.850
I asked the president, 
and she got one especially for you.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.590
The girl with the golden drills?

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.850
The president's pretty nice, after all.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:21.510
Oh, right!

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:24.250
Actually, there's something 
I've been worried about.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.610
Worried about?

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.740
I checked your fortune just now,

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.200
and it seems you need to watch out
 for women and water.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.070
Women and water?

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:38.490
Yeah. So make sure you're really careful 
with water, and especially women.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.270
Sure. Got it.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.830
Hm? Is there something else?

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:47.840
If you could...

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:50.560
...try to get me Sakura-san's autograph!

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.930
Hayato. Hayato.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:58.430
Good morning. 
We've made it to the Zwei Islands.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.520
Emile! You're here again?!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.390
We don't make shore very often.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.230
I wanted to go on a date with you.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:10.400
You don't have anything to do 
in the morning, right?

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:17.240
Sorry, I got word yesterday that the mission 
will begin in the morning instead.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.730
What?!

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:19.540
Sorry.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.080
I see.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.970
Oh, well. Work is work.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.650
That really sucks, though.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.220
Good luck today.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:40.270
Kisaragi Hayato, are you ready?

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.730
Yes. I've got my tracer and N-tranquilizers

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.310
right here.

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:48.960
This'll be your first bodyguard 
mission. Keep alert.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:49.740
Right.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:05.340
I'm so happy I could come back.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.050
Nice to meet you.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.980
I'm the XO on the <i>Little Garden,</i>

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.290
Liddy Steinberg.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.420
I'm Kirishima Sakura.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.010
Nice to meet you.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:20.090
So you're Kisaragi Hayato-san, right?

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:23.020
Nice to meet you.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.740
Nice to meet you.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:35.980
Is it always like this?

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:38.750
No, this is actually light.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:39.540
Seriously?

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:46.610
<i>Why did someone so famous 
want me as a bodyguard?</i>

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:48.880
What's the matter?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.210
Nothing at all.

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:55.340
Do you have a favorite song of mine?

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:58.150
Uh... well...

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:01.220
I'm sorry. I don't listen to much music.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:02.780
I see.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:06.740
But my sister's a fan. An ardententent...

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:07.710
Huh?

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.060
You really don't have it together, do you?

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:15.740
It's okay. I don't mind.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:19.320
Oh, and you don't have to try to be so polite.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:23.120
Forget the formalities,
and just call me "Sakura."

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:36.900
Here you go.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:39.860
You're not going in?

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:45.170
I believe there's something
you need to do first, as my bodyguard.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:47.060
Ah, yeah. I should check the room.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.290
Let's see... The tracer...

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:51.360
Here it is.

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:55.920
Are you really <i>the</i> Kisaragi Hayato?

00:09:56.850 --> 00:10:00.320
W-Well, that is my name...

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:05.340
But uh... I've never been a bodyguard before.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:08.080
Sorry, I'll do my check. Hold on a second.

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:13.210
All clear. You can come in.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.600
Looks like we finally get some time alone.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.090
Hey, Hayato.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.450
Wanna get married?

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.650
Hey, Hayato.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:37.530
Wanna get married?

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.520
This is you, right?

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.030
Why do you...

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.450
I found it on the Cybernet.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.510
Though it's been erased now.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.890
I saw this and took an interest in you...

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.910
The hero who saved the Zwei Islands.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:58.330
You're a little different than I expected.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.470
You're pretty awkward.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:04.210
But I think that's pretty cute.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:04.810
What?

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:08.630
Hey, want to go out? 
With an eye on getting married, of course.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:09.810
Wh-Why?

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:13.930
Hm? You're not happy I'm hitting on you?

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:17.230
Do you have someone already?

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:19.490
Do you?

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.430
H-Hold on a second.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:23.780
Why are you talking about going out?

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:29.790
The miracle couple: the Diva of the World 
and the Genius Slayer.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.460
Wouldn't that be great?

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.630
I think the media would eat it up, too.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.500
Huh? The media...?

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.170
We'd hold a press conference, right?

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:43.510
We'd use the Zwei Islands, 
the place we met, for the location.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.720
I'd have on a ring you got me 
using three months' worth of pay.

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:48.550
Uh, Sakura...

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:50.980
After the press conference
comes the ceremony.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:50.980
Huh?!

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.190
It'd have a minimum of 
five outfit changes for us.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.360
We're both from Yamato,
so white kimonos would be perfect!

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.860
The honeymoon would be
a trip around the world, obviously.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:58.860
Hey, you listening?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:02.110
And then we'd move into a white house 
by the ocean together.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.520
We'd have three kids and two dogs.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:06.660
On our days off, we'd all play in the water,

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.570
and there'd be a rainbow in the sky...

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:11.100
<i>This is hopeless. 
The brakes have come off her train of thought.</i>

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:12.370
I need to do something...

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.700
Sounds good. Let's go out.

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:15.410
Huh?

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:18.940
We'll have the press conference, 
do all the changing at the wedding,

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:21.900
go on that honeymoon, and live happily
 ever after with our kids and dogs,

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.380
and a rainbow in the sky.

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:29.140
So how about we kiss to seal the deal?

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:35.950
W-Wait!

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:39.020
I-I actually don't have
much time to get ready.

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:41.690
So I'm going to stop teasing you,
and go take a bath.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:59.290
She's pretty good.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.090
Karen used to sing in the bath
when she was younger, too.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.360
Hayato-kun.

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:07.930
What is it?

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.630
Could you get me my PDA?

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:14.060
I just thought of a good musical phrase. 
I want to record it.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:15.490
Sure.

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:25.950
<i>Karen left her stuff all over 
when she was young, too.</i>

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.290
Hayato-kun, have you found it yet?

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:29.700
What are you—?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.580
Oh, I just wanted to tidy everything up...

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:36.750
Never mind that! 
Just give me my PDA—

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:41.160
Are you okay?!

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.850
Ow...

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:50.260
H-Here.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:52.100
Th-Thanks.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.570
Also, the bear is an exception.

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.810
It's not like I'm into that or anything.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.810
That was bad.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:02.790
Wait a second...

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.220
Women and water... Was that 
what Karen was talking about?

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:06.620
Hayato-kun.

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:08.950
How do I look?

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:09.950
Huh?

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.080
What do you think?

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.960
I-It's cute, I guess.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:20.670
That answer gets forty out of hundred.

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:22.640
Forty points?

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.240
What about what happened in the bathroom?

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.660
Uh, well...

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.130
I'm sorry.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:29.840
Fifteen points.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.850
What do I need to say 
to get a passing grade?

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:36.730
Be a man and figure it out yourself.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.470
Let's go. It's time to leave.

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:40.940
Y-Yeah.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:58.410
What's wrong?

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:03.480
I think it's impressive you can handle 
everyone so effortlessly like that.

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:07.750
Then I'm even more impressive 
than you think.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:08.420
Huh?

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:11.580
Souffle, we're done here for today, right?

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:12.510
Yes.

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:16.000
Then let's take a little detour.

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:23.150
What is this?

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:26.160
The stage for the next concert.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:29.330
We expect 100,000 people to come.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:30.150
100,000?!

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:34.200
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:37.510
Did you figure it out?

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:39.410
No, I'm not looking at your boobs.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:42.330
Boobs? What are you going on about?

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.170
I knew you were dense.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.240
Hayato-kun,

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:49.060
I'm trying to say that this 
is my battlefield.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:50.300
I'll show you.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.140
Hundred On!

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:10.590
A Slayer...

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.110
This is my Hundred:

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.500
Fairy Fairytale.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.620
She's flying.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:30.340
Impressive, as always.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:35.200
Oh, Professor Charlotte. 
Mei-Mai's here, too.

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:36.900
Why are you two here?

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:40.370
She's going to use her Hundred 
as part of her concert,

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:42.350
so we were called here to help.

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:44.970
Her type is incredibly rare.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:47.620
She's a field-control type Slayer.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.610
Field-control type...

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:53.230
She can create a personal field
over a specific period of time

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:58.590
and use her sense energy 
to fly around and create illusions.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:01.620
But she also can't create any weapons.

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:06.290
She doesn't need any weapons 
to fight her fight, though.

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:09.760
That's right. She has her song.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.760
Do you two know each other?

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:14.480
We used to be colleagues.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:18.510
You could also say Charlotte
 saved Sakura's life.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.090
Her life...

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:24.360
I just helped her when she was 
caught up in a tough situation.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:26.490
It wasn't that big of a deal.

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:41.200
What do you think of my stage, Hayato-kun?

00:17:41.550 --> 00:17:44.040
It's amazing. It really is!

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:45.430
Of course it is.

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:48.210
I'm the Diva of the World.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.490
In order to repay my fans,
who have been waiting for this day,

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:54.340
and the staff that helped
put together this stage,

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.260
I need to put on the best concert possible.

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.330
It'll be great.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.580
Sakura...

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:06.520
Yes, we're done for today.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.520
They said I could come back 
in the afternoon tomorrow.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:12.550
<i>But the plan was for you to
start in the morning tomorrow, too.</i>

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:17.190
She has a song she needs to 
stay in the hotel to write.

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:21.890
Sakura was complaining that she 
wanted to go somewhere, but...

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:23.270
<i>Sakura?</i>

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:25.700
<i>You're calling your client "Sakura"?</i>

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.670
Well, Kirishima-san 
told me to call her that...

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.670
If that's what the client wanted...

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:36.570
Come to my summer home 
tomorrow morning, then.

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:38.180
There's something I'd like 
to talk to you about.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:40.270
I understand.

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:41.700
<i>I can't wait—</i>

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:44.030
<i>I mean, I'll be waiting.</i>

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:44.740
Huh?

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:50.810
Is everyone still on the island?

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:52.610
I guess that means

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:54.860
I get to be the first in the bath!

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:57.420
Huh?

00:18:57.420 --> 00:18:58.280
It's locked.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:01.700
Oh, it opened up.

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:11.080
Haya...to?

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:13.180
Emile, why are you...

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:14.840
I'm sorry.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:15.730
Wait.

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:21.590
Want to take a bath with me?

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:22.920
Huh?

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:27.580
I used my security code to lock the door,

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:30.280
so I was under the impression 
no one could get in, but...

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:34.280
We were in the same room, 
so I guess our keys are the same, too.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:37.200
You still haven't gotten a new one?

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.990
If I changed it out, I wouldn't be 
able to get in your room anymore.

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:42.570
Hey...

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:45.090
So how was your first mission?

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:47.230
I think it went all right.

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:48.790
There was a bit of trouble partway through,

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:50.120
but Sakura was okay with—

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.260
Sakura?!

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:53.980
You're calling her "Sakura"?! 
What's that about?

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:55.630
Call me by my name, too!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.070
What do you mean?

00:19:58.120 --> 00:19:59.630
I always do.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.430
Not that!

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.030
My real name...

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:12.730
Emilia...

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:15.490
One more time.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.360
Emilia.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:19.620
Yeah.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.050
Hayato, look.

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:28.980
Here, at my scar.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:31.450
It's starting to fade away.

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:32.500
Huh?

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:35.990
It wasn't going away at all before.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:42.260
But I guess seeing you again and
feeling better about things did the trick.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:49.140
Hey, you don't have to look 
so closely, you know?

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.300
You've got this pervy look on your face.

00:20:58.300 --> 00:21:02.080
Emilia, you want to come to 
the Zwei Islands tomorrow?

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.030
Are you sure? 
What about your mission?

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:07.140
I start in the afternoon tomorrow.

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:10.950
Once I go finish things up with the president 
in the morning, I'm free until the afternoon.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:15.500
Yay! Thank you, Hayato!

00:21:22.350 --> 00:21:23.970
Hayato, you perv!

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:29.060
Women and water...

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:30.940
Again.

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:42.330
Please let my song reach everyone.

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:46.300
And someday... that person, too...

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:53.000
Looks like security's pretty tight 
this time, just as Vitaly said.

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:57.580
But <i>Little Garden</i> Slayers are
hardly gonna give us any trouble.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:21:58.250
Let's go.

00:21:58.250 --> 00:21:59.590
Well, hold your horses.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:02.660
Make do with this for today.

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:07.830
So when are we doing it?

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:12.430
After the concert.

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:17.620
Yeah. The islanders are all excited,
so let them have their fun.

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:23.430
After all, we're on humanity's side.

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:05.870
<b>Imitation Girl</b>
